{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"7ebeffa84d86190a","name":"card_unit_43_infantry_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/Homefront/units/card_unit_43_infantry_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"43. INFANTRY REGIMENT","text":"At the end of your turn, draw the top card of your deck if it has even cost.","flavorText":"The 43rd Infantry Regiment was part of the German 1st Infantry Division, formed in 1935 from elements of the old Reichswehr. Stationed in Insterburg, East Prussia, it drew its recruits largely from this region and inherited a strong Prussian identity. The division participated in the 1939 invasion of Poland, seeing action at Mława and during the siege of Warsaw. In 1940 it fought in the Battle of France, and it was later committed to Operation Barbarossa, advancing into the Soviet Union in 1941. It took part in the siege of Leningrad and remained active on the Eastern Front throughout the war. The 1st Infantry Division endured repeated Soviet offensives, including the encirclement at Kamenets-Podolsky in 1944. Despite heavy casualties, it continued to operate until the division’s final surrender in May 1945.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.bond"],"Name":"card_unit_43_infantry_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_43_infantry_regiment_title","SourceString":"43. INFANTRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"43. INFANTRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_43_infantry_regiment_text","SourceString":"At the end of your turn, draw the top card of your deck if it has even cost.","LocalizedString":"At the end of your turn, draw the top card of your deck if it has even cost."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_43_infantry_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 43rd Infantry Regiment was part of the German 1st Infantry Division, formed in 1935 from elements of the old Reichswehr. Stationed in Insterburg, East Prussia, it drew its recruits largely from this region and inherited a strong Prussian identity. The division participated in the 1939 invasion of Poland, seeing action at Mława and during the siege of Warsaw. In 1940 it fought in the Battle of France, and it was later committed to Operation Barbarossa, advancing into the Soviet Union in 1941. It took part in the siege of Leningrad and remained active on the Eastern Front throughout the war. The 1st Infantry Division endured repeated Soviet offensives, including the encirclement at Kamenets-Podolsky in 1944. Despite heavy casualties, it continued to operate until the division’s final surrender in May 1945.","LocalizedString":"The 43rd Infantry Regiment was part of the German 1st Infantry Division, formed in 1935 from elements of the old Reichswehr. Stationed in Insterburg, East Prussia, it drew its recruits largely from this region and inherited a strong Prussian identity. The division participated in the 1939 invasion of Poland, seeing action at Mława and during the siege of Warsaw. In 1940 it fought in the Battle of France, and it was later committed to Operation Barbarossa, advancing into the Soviet Union in 1941. It took part in the siege of Leningrad and remained active on the Eastern Front throughout the war. The 1st Infantry Division endured repeated Soviet offensives, including the encirclement at Kamenets-Podolsky in 1944. Despite heavy casualties, it continued to operate until the division’s final surrender in May 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/43__INFANTRY_REGIMENT.43__INFANTRY_R